{"schemaVersion":1,"workId":"OL262454W","title":"The Hound of the Baskervilles","authors":["Arthur Conan Doyle"],"firstPublished":1900,"edition":{"description":"Sections as detected in Project Gutenberg eBook #2852.","source":"Project Gutenberg eBook #2852","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/2852"},"sectionLabel":{"singular":"Chapter","plural":"Chapters"},"sections":[{"id":"s1","label":"Ch. 1","title":"Mr. Sherlock Holmes"},{"id":"s2","label":"Ch. 2","title":"The Curse of the Baskervilles"},{"id":"s3","label":"Ch. 3","title":"The Problem"},{"id":"s4","label":"Ch. 4","title":"Sir Henry Baskerville"},{"id":"s5","label":"Ch. 5","title":"Three Broken Threads"},{"id":"s6","label":"Ch. 6","title":"Baskerville Hall"},{"id":"s7","label":"Ch. 7","title":"The Stapletons of Merripit House"},{"id":"s8","label":"Ch. 8","title":"First Report of Dr. Watson"},{"id":"s9","label":"Ch. 9","title":"The Light upon the Moor [Second Report of Dr. Watson]"},{"id":"s10","label":"Ch. 10","title":"Extract from the Diary of Dr. Watson"},{"id":"s11","label":"Ch. 11","title":"The Man on the Tor"},{"id":"s12","label":"Ch. 12","title":"Death on the Moor"},{"id":"s13","label":"Ch. 13","title":"Fixing the Nets"},{"id":"s14","label":"Ch. 14","title":"The Hound of the Baskervilles"},{"id":"s15","label":"Ch. 15","title":"A Retrospection"}],"groups":[{"id":"g-stapleton","label":"Stapleton (shared surname)"},{"id":"g-lyons","label":"Lyons (shared surname)"},{"id":"g-barrymore","label":"Barrymore (shared surname)"}],"characters":[{"id":"sherlock-holmes","name":"Sherlock Holmes","aliases":["Holmes","Mr. Holmes","Mr. Sherlock Holmes"],"role":"protagonist","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “Mr.”"},{"id":"sir-henry-baskerville","name":"Sir Henry","aliases":["Sir Henry Baskerville"],"role":"protagonist","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: ““By advising me as to what I should do with Sir Henry Baskerville, who arrives at Waterloo Station”—Dr.”"},{"id":"watson","name":"Watson","aliases":["Dr. Watson"],"role":"protagonist","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: ““Well, Watson, what do you make of it?””"},{"id":"sir-charles-baskerville","name":"Sir Charles","aliases":["Sir Charles Baskerville","Charles"],"role":"major","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: ““This family paper was committed to my care by Sir Charles Baskerville, whose sudden and tragic death some three months ago created so much excitement in Devonshire.”"},{"id":"dr-mortimer","name":"Dr. Mortimer","aliases":["Mortimer"],"role":"major","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: ““To James Mortimer, M.R.C.S., from his friends of the C.C.H.,” was engraved upon it, with the date “1884.”"},{"id":"hugo-baskerville","name":"Hugo Baskerville","aliases":["Hugo"],"role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: ““Of the origin of the Hound of the Baskervilles there have been many statements, yet as I come in a direct line from Hugo Baskerville, and as I had the story from my father, who also had it from his, I have set it dow…”"},{"id":"selden","name":"Selden","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s6","summary":"First mention: ““It is Selden, the Notting Hill murderer.””"},{"id":"frankland","name":"Frankland","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s8","summary":"First mention: “Mortimer, and Frankland, of Lafter Hall, let me end on that which is most important and tell you more about the Barrymores, and especially about the surprising development of last night.”"},{"id":"miss-stapleton","name":"Miss Stapleton","role":"minor","group":"g-stapleton","firstAppearance":"s7","summary":"First mention: “I could not doubt that this was the Miss Stapleton of whom I had been told, since ladies of any sort must be few upon the moor, and I remembered that I had heard someone describe her as being a beauty.”"},{"id":"mrs-laura-lyons","name":"Mrs. Laura Lyons","role":"minor","group":"g-lyons","firstAppearance":"s10","summary":"First mention: “Tomorrow morning I shall find my way to Coombe Tracey, and if I can see this Mrs.”"},{"id":"mrs-lyons","name":"Mrs. Lyons","role":"minor","group":"g-lyons","firstAppearance":"s11","summary":"First mention: “I had no opportunity to tell the baronet what I had learned about Mrs.”"},{"id":"lestrade","name":"Lestrade","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s13","summary":"First mention: “Lestrade.”"},{"id":"cartwright","name":"Cartwright","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s4","summary":"First mention: “I have some recollection, Wilson, that you had among your boys a lad named Cartwright, who showed some ability during the investigation.””"},{"id":"mrs-stapleton","name":"Mrs. Stapleton","role":"minor","group":"g-stapleton","firstAppearance":"s14","summary":"First mention: “In a minute we had torn off the gag, unswathed the bonds, and Mrs.”"},{"id":"mr-stapleton","name":"Mr. Stapleton","role":"minor","group":"g-stapleton","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “Frankland, of Lafter Hall, and Mr.”"},{"id":"mr-barrymore","name":"Mr. Barrymore","role":"minor","group":"g-barrymore","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “Address to Mr.”"},{"id":"perkins","name":"Perkins","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: ““On the night of Sir Charles’s death Barrymore the butler, who made the discovery, sent Perkins the groom on horseback to me, and as I was sitting up late I was able to reach Baskerville Hall within an hour of the event.”"},{"id":"mrs-barrymore","name":"Mrs. Barrymore","role":"minor","group":"g-barrymore","firstAppearance":"s7","summary":"First mention: “And yet he lied as he said it, for it chanced that after breakfast I met Mrs.”"}],"relationships":[{"id":"r1","source":"dr-mortimer","target":"sherlock-holmes","weight":46,"phases":[{"at":"s1","type":"together","label":"Appear together","weight":6,"note":"First named together in Ch. 1."},{"at":"s2","type":"together","label":"Often together","weight":14},{"at":"s7","type":"together","label":"Constantl